GENERATE_STAGE_EPISODE_PLAN_PROMPT = '\nAs the series-structure writer, assign episode ranges to the given story phases based on the detailed events, causal relationships, emotional progression, and appropriate pacing. Plan ranges only; do not write episode outlines. Total episodes: {{TotalEpisodeNums}}.\n\n## Genre\n{{Topic}}\n## World\n{{WorldView}}\n## Story premise\n{{StoryOutline}}\n## Characters\n{{RoleInfo}}\n## Detailed series outline\n{{FullOutline}}\n## Ordered phases and events\n{{Stages}}\n\nRequirements:\n1. Keep the phases in the supplied order and give each at least one episode. Ranges must start at episode 1, be continuous and non-overlapping, and end at episode {{TotalEpisodeNums}}. Do not omit, add, rename, or repeat a phase.\n2. Allocate space according to event complexity, escalating conflict, emotional turns, and dramatic development rather than dividing mechanically by event count. For serialized short-form drama, aim to bring the protagonist’s urgent goal and central conflict into focus early. Allocate the development episodes to sustain momentum through escalating obstacles and meaningful changes in the situation. Give pivotal revelations, reversals, and emotional payoffs enough room for their setup and consequences, balancing compact pacing with clear causality.\n3. Establish the characters and central conflict in Setup, allow sufficient room for Development and Climax to unfold, and resolve the story plausibly in Resolution. Do not conclude the main storyline\'s central climax prematurely and then introduce a new main storyline to fill the remaining episodes. Assign each event only once.\n4. Briefly explain each pacing allocation without rewriting the event line.\n\n{% if RetryFeedback %}The previous output failed validation. Correct it: {{RetryFeedback}}{% endif %}\nOutput a JSON array only:\n[\n  {"stage": "Original phase name", "start_episode_id": 1, "end_episode_id": 3, "pacing_reason": "Reason based on story content and pacing"}\n]\n'
